  "id": "COMPOUND:8058 - PROTEIN:1806",
  "verbalization": "Stiripentol is implicated in targeting multiple entities, including Far upstream element-binding protein 1, Keratin, type II cytoskeletal 1, and Complement factor B, all of which are targets of other molecules. These targets are linked to Selenoprotein P through a series of indirect relationships, suggesting that stiripentol may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence points to Selenoprotein P as a downstream target of several unrelated molecules, which may indicate that the drug's mechanism involves modulating pathways that ultimately influence Selenoprotein P. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on Selenoprotein P suggests a potential role in cellular processes that are regulated by these targets. While the exact mechanism by which stiripentol affects Selenoprotein P remains unclear, the integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that the drug interacts with a broader set of molecular components that ultimately influence Selenoprotein P through indirect pathways.",
